{"questions":[{"question_id":"pe3VuSMjafKGXbUY","paperTitle":"AIEEE 2004","year":2004,"examDate":2004,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"hydrocarbons","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","topic":"properties-and-preparation-of-alkanes","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"which-one-of-the-following-has-the-minimum-boiling-point-2004-marks-4-pe3vusmjafkgxbuy.htm","content":"Which one of the following has the minimum boiling point?","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"n-butane"},{"identifier":"B","content":"isobutane"},{"identifier":"C","content":"1- butene "},{"identifier":"D","content":"1- butyne "}],"correct_options":["B"],"explanation":"<b>NOTE :</b> Among isomeric alkanes, the straight chain isomer has higher boiling point than  the branched chain isomer. The greater the branching of the chain, the lower is the boiling point. Further due to the presence of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.296ex\" height=\"1ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -431 573 442\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D70B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D70B\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> electrons, these molecules are slightly polar and hence have higher boiling points than the corresponding alkanes. \n<br><br>Thus <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.439ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.93ex\" height=\"1.984ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 2179 877\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(759,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1037,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D45D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1540,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1901,0)\"><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> follows the order\n<br><br>alkynes <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.09ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.312ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -540 778 580\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> alkene <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.09ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.312ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -540 778 580\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"3E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3E\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>  alkanes (straight chain) &gt; branched chain alkanes. "}]}